      "content": "i see what u mean about the historical context. but if i'm aiming for a high-quality sociology curriculum, shouldn't i follow the standard academic approach of presenting multiple sociological theories neutrally? if i just tell the students to \"dismantle\" one side, won't that be seen as indoctrination rather than teaching them how to think critically about different social models?",
